From bbc385271f651808b2ddd1549a072370fa7b13d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: l4h <z@univalence.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:32:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] mcs: add per-TCB deadline timers (seL4_TCB_SetTimer)

Allow user level to arm a one-shot, absolute deadline timer that signals a
badge to the TCB's bound notification when it expires. Armed timers are
kept in a per-core queue sorted by deadline, and the queue head is taken
into account when programming the MCS kernel's one-shot timer, so no
additional hardware timer is needed.

This gives user-level OS personalities (e.g. paravirtualised guest
kernels) a cheap clock-event device on platforms without a spare timer
device such as cloud VMs without HPET.
